1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,800
Two ways into Tibet, and they're nothing alike. I'm your China Travel Expert.

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:07,000
One is the highest railway on Earth.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,400
The Qinghai–Tibet line climbs to 5,072 m, oxygen piped into every carriage.

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,800
1,956 km of track, much of it above 4,000 m.

5
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:16,800
The other way is the G318 — days of driving over the plateau.

6
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,600
Double-tap if you'd take the train.

7
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:23,600
★ Expert Tip: Spend a night at Xining or Golmud first — let your body meet the altitude.

8
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:27,200
Highest railway on Earth, or the G318 drive — which way to Lhasa?
